// Every item of the game. `display` is a row of ItemDisplayInfo.dbc: it gives the icon, the textures painted on the
// character (armor) and the model held in the hand (weapons and shields), so a worn item always shows on the character.
// Ids are what other files and saves refer to; do not rename them. `buy` is what a merchant asks (copper) and `sell` what
// one pays; an item with no `sell` cannot be sold. `quest: true` marks a quest item: it drops only while a quest being worked on still\n// wants it, says "Quest Item" in its tooltip and, like in the original, is not sold. Left out: quality 1 (common), stack 1, no stats.
[
    (id: "longsword", name: "Squire's Longsword", display: 12274, class: 2, sub: 7, wear: OneHand, kind: ("One-Hand", "Sword"), weapon: Some((min: 10.0, max: 14.0, speed: 2.6)), handling: "MetalLarge", buy: 450, sell: 90),
